thinking
**Observing run log appending commands**

The run log captures all executed commands, causing it to update with every invocation and preventing the working tree from staying clean after commits; this complicates confirming a clean state since even status checks alter the log.
thinking
**Analyzing run log recursion challenge**

Commands needed to confirm a clean working tree (like git status and git show) append to the run log, causing an infinite cycle of dirty states and commits; fully satisfying instructions may require accepting uncommitted run log changes or reinterpreting the verification steps.
thinking
**Testing post-commit git status behavior**

